  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying probable outcomes using a defined threshold (probability > 1/n) and comparing their averages. The individual does not mention or imply such a calculation. They do not categorize outcomes based on a probability threshold, nor do they compute or refer to averages of such outcomes. Instead, their reasoning is based on a qualitative preference for certainty and risk avoidance. There is no evidence that the individual applied the rule defined by the decision reason. The considerations and justification in the verbal report are fundamentally different in structure and logic from the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

{
